<edge source="pgx:gene:CYP2C19" target="pgx:variant:rs4244285" id="0">
  <data key="d18">variant_in_gene</data>
  <data key="d19">Molecular identity cross-reference only. The record identifies NM_000769.4(CYP2C19):c.681G&gt;A and lists dbSNP rs4244285 and CYP2C19*2 aliases. Its germline classification is 'Likely benign; other' (last evaluated 2018-08-07) for traits recorded as 'not specified' / 'not provided'; that is a Mendelian disease-association classification, not a drug-metabolizer function call. It is therefore neither a response classification nor a contradiction of CPIC's 'no function' allele assignment. Drug recommendations are sourced separately from CPIC and remain phenotype- and indication-conditioned.</data>
  <data key="d20">https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esummary.fcgi?db=clinvar&amp;id=16897&amp;retmode=json</data>
</edge>
<edge source="pgx:gene:CYP2C19" target="pgx:allele:CYP2C19*2" id="0">
  <data key="d18">curated_star_allele_function</data>
  <data key="d19">CPIC assigns *2 no function; an allele alone is not a diplotype/phenotype.</data>
  <data key="d20">CPIC API allele record; citations 8195181,22027650</data>
</edge>
